course: dictionary
lesson: 8220
title: Reveal and its clues
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To reveal something is to show what was hidden, or to tell people a fact they did not know. The words around the word give you the clue. «Revealing the danger too fast removes the suspense.» Suspense is the feeling of waiting to find out what happens, so revealing the danger early means showing it before the reader is ready.
explain: «And the Rat reveals he caught the invitations in time.» The Rat tells Mole a fact Mole did not know, so reveal here means tell. Check your meaning by swapping in show or tell. If the sentence still makes sense, your meaning is right.
explain: «Joseph revealed himself, wept and forgave his brothers.» Joseph had been hidden from his brothers, and now they saw who he really was. Reveal often has this sense of showing what was hidden, but it can also mean telling a secret.
fact: Reveal means to show something that was hidden, or to tell a secret or fact that people did not know.
fact: Reveal is a verb: reveal, reveals, revealed, revealing.
fact: In stories, the ending often reveals a secret or who did it.
fact: In science, experiments reveal facts about the world.
fact: Never reveal personal information, such as your address or passwords, online.
exercise: «Revealing the danger too fast removes the suspense.» What does reveal mean here? | To make a loud noise before the danger | To run away from the danger | *To show or tell something early, so it is no longer hidden | To hide the danger carefully
exercise: «Joseph revealed himself, wept and forgave his brothers.» What did Joseph reveal? | The way home | *Who he really was | The food he had cooked | A new coat
exercise: Mia says, «Never reveal your password online.» What should you do? | Share it with your whole class | Tell it to strangers online | Write it on a public website | *Keep it private
test: «The Rat reveals he caught the invitations in time.» What does reveals mean? | To post the letters without reading them | *To tell Mole a fact he did not know | To hide the invitations | To lose the letters
test: In an informal way, what is a reveal? | A type of bird | A kind of cake | A loud argument | *A big moment when something hidden is shown
exam: «Joseph revealed himself, wept and forgave his brothers.» What is the best meaning of revealed here? | *Showed who he really was, after hiding it | Shouted at | Lost track of | Gave away his money
